  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on the first run (3 witnesses, 3 atoms read), so 5 of the 6 runs are left unused.\n\n**Body:** `rises (turning_right(a; yaw_tolerance, speed_tolerance) ∧ headingSince(a, step, turning_right(a; …)) ≤ −turn_angle)`\n\nThis is the accepted `left_turn_from_onset` concept turned to the other hand, with the comparison against the negative of the turn angle. It does what the contract asks:\n- **Recognition:** it holds only at the observation where the heading change since the onset first reaches −turn_angle. That can be the onset itself, if zero already reaches it.\n- **Earlier stretches:** a turn built up over an earlier stretch doesn't count, because each new start of `turning_right` resets the heading change to zero.\n- **Unknown cases:** it is unknown when the onset wasn't observed or a yaw rate is missing.\n\nThe contract left nothing open, so I declared no narrowings.\n\n**Witnesses** (turn angle 60°, yaw tolerance 2°/s, speed tolerance 0.1 m/s, step 2 s, one observation per second):\n- **holds:** a short right yaw at 2–3 s, straight at 4 s, then a second stretch at 5–7 s that turns a quarter turn. Measured from the second onset, the heading change reaches the angle at 7000 ms, the scenario's window. Counted from the first onset it would already reach it at 6000 ms, so the scenario tells the two stretches apart, as the record's narrative requires.\n- **fails:** a lane-change drift that never gets near −60°.\n- **blind:** the same trace as `holds` with `kin.yaw_rate` hidden, checked at 7000 ms.\n\nFiles are in `/local-scratch2/sma407/smoke32-run/pipeline/traffic-spec-agent`:\n- `library/TrafficSpec/Concepts/motion/right_turn_from_onset.lean`\n- `library/TrafficSpecWitness/Concepts/motion/right_turn_from_onset.lean`\n- `results/smoke32-1111-2102/iter-002/code/concept__drv_motion_right_turn_from_onset/task_result.md`",
